wbanish 0.2.0: new package, ITP #NNNNNN

wbanish hides the mouse cursor while typing on Wayland, like xbanish does
on X11. It is a binary-only crate; the binary package is "wbanish".

All dependencies are already in unstable at the required versions:
evdev 0.13.2, rustix 1.1.4, signal-hook 0.4.4, wayland-client 0.31.15,
wayland-protocols 0.32.13 (client, staging, unstable features) and
wayland-protocols-wlr 0.3.12.

Test-built with debcargo 2.8.4 and dpkg-buildpackage in a clean unstable
container, using only Debian's librust-*-dev packages; the package builds,
installs and runs. The binary package also ships the GNOME Shell
extension that wbanish uses on GNOME.

I am the upstream author and would appreciate a review and a sponsor.
